(Leonard:)Uh, so, what would you
like to know?

13
00:00:29,310 --> 00:00:33,020
(Page:)You work with Mr. Wolowitz here
at the university, correct?

14
00:00:33,020 --> 00:00:35,350
(Leonard:)Yes. Of course, we're in
different departments.

15
00:00:35,350 --> 00:00:37,550
(Leonard:)He's an engineer and I'm
an experimental physicist.

16
00:00:37,550 --> 00:00:39,020
(Leonard:)You know, one
of those guys

17
00:00:39,020 --> 00:00:41,590
(Leonard:)who examines the building blocks
of creation

18
00:00:41,590 --> 00:00:45,660
(Leonard:)and says,
"Hello, maker of the universe.

19
00:00:45,660 --> 00:00:48,130
"I see what you did there.

20
00:00:48,130 --> 00:00:49,830
Good one."

21
00:00:49,830 --> 00:00:51,470
(Woman at Door:)Right.

22
00:00:51,470 --> 00:00:52,740
(Page:)Now, how would you characterize

23
00:00:52,740 --> 00:00:54,800
(Page:)your relationship
with Mr. Wolowitz?

24
00:00:54,810 --> 00:00:56,940
(Howard:)Good.

25
00:00:56,940 --> 00:00:59,580
(Leonard:)It's a good
relationship.

26
00:00:59,580 --> 00:01:02,780
(Leonard:)Of course, most of my
relationships are good.

